WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:02.784
- It baffles me how many people

00:00:02.784 --> 00:00:05.634
think that they're bigger
than they actually are.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.384
(dramatic music)

00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:11.861
I hear people say like,

00:00:11.861 --> 00:00:13.562
well how do I get in 
the New York Times?

00:00:13.562 --> 00:00:16.350
Or how do I get that
meeting with that CEO?

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.517
And often times I just say,
one is better than zero.

00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:27.520
The steps it takes 
to actually get

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.722
to the biggest 
places in the world.

00:00:29.722 --> 00:00:31.847
Before you getting a
meeting with, you know,

00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:35.237
Zucks or Cuban or Barry Diller

00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:36.146
or whoever you're trying to have

00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:37.560
a meeting with 
in the business world,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.245
well you've got to have
a lot of little meetings

00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:40.767
to build up your cadence.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.999
People are always like
man, you've been on Conan

00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:45.970
and Ellen and the Today Show

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.630
and CNN and Fox,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.112
like how do I get that?

00:00:50.112 --> 00:00:53.291
And I'm like well, I also
did a thousand interviews

00:00:53.291 --> 00:00:58.718
it feels like on videos that
got one or 19 or 137 views.

00:00:58.721 --> 00:01:01.560
Like my PR people and all
my managers and handlers

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.916
are really pissed at me
because they're like,

00:01:03.916 --> 00:01:06.858
why are we spending 15
minutes doing these blogs

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:10.181
that have six readers,
you know, every single day

00:01:10.181 --> 00:01:12.324
and you're passing on the
stuff that we're giving you

00:01:12.324 --> 00:01:14.302
to be on CNN or New York Times?

00:01:14.302 --> 00:01:17.098
I still, even today, am as happy

00:01:17.098 --> 00:01:19.601
and sometimes even more
excited to be on a podcast

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.055
or a video blog that's only
going to reach 100 people

00:01:22.055 --> 00:01:24.187
because I'm always about
depth versus width.

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:26.257
Do you want to go wide or
do you want to go deep?

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:27.833
I want to go deeper 
with my community.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:30.297
I want to give back to
people that were fans of me.

00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:33.113
And so even today, where
I have more leverage than I did

00:01:33.113 --> 00:01:34.696
three or four, 
five to six years ago,

00:01:34.696 --> 00:01:36.945
to get bigger platforms, 
I still live

00:01:36.945 --> 00:01:39.725
under the motto of one
is better than zero.

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:42.389
To me, doing these interviews
is a process of the work

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:45.594
that so many people are
impatient and not willing to do.

00:01:45.594 --> 00:01:48.679
Are you willing to take 10
minutes to get 195 views?

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:50.719
I am. I don't know 
who you think you are.

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:53.345
You've not gotten the exposure yet.

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:56.214
When you have not 
made your name just yet,

00:01:56.214 --> 00:01:57.961
when you're still 
making the climb,

00:01:57.961 --> 00:01:59.530
when you're not paying attention

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.495
'cause nobody else is, 'cause
217 people watched the video,

00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:04.180
I'm grinding when you're sleeping.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.312
I did those 87s and 59s
and 137s and 813 views

00:02:08.312 --> 00:02:10.560
day in and day out, day in and
day out, day in and day out

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.824
and continued to.

00:02:11.824 --> 00:02:14.172
You might make a video
on somebody's video show

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:17.964
that has 89 viewers, but
one of those 89 viewers

00:02:17.964 --> 00:02:21.713
may be a producer at
CNN or might be the CFO

00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:23.800
of a big company that
you're trying to reach,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.129
and so undervaluing 
just that one view,

00:02:26.129 --> 00:02:27.408
it needs to be the right view,

00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:29.980
but it's one view,
is a humongous mistake.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.437
It's about having the humility.

00:02:32.437 --> 00:02:35.368
It's about not saying no,
even when you've made it.

00:02:35.368 --> 00:02:38.897
And that the one is
greater than zero concept

00:02:38.897 --> 00:02:42.634
is something I'm proud that
I continue to execute on.

